{
  "version": 1,
  "_schema": "despia-colorpicker-resolution-v1",
  "_note": "The U07 <colorpicker> pure core: the hex round-trip (3/4/6/8 digits in, #RRGGBB or #RRGGBBAA out), swatch normalisation, the mode default, and THE NAME TABLE \u2014 the picker announces the selected colour by NAME, not just by hex, because '#0A84FF' read aloud is not a colour. Nearest name is squared sRGB distance with ties broken by table order, pinned so three renderers announce the same word.",
